   "k": "final summary all",
   "v": "BRCA1 is associated with familial cancer of breast, familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1, pancreatic cancer susceptibility 4, and Fanconi anemia complementation group S.⁠1–4 | Found 4 disease records for BRCA1: Familial cancer of breast, Familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1, Pancreatic cancer susceptibility 4 and Fanconi anemia complementation group S.⁠1–4 | BRCA1 mutations are responsible for approximately 40% of inherited breast cancers and more than 80% of inherited breast and ovarian cancers.⁠23 | The gene encodes a 190 kD nuclear phosphoprotein that plays a role in maintaining genomic stability, and it also acts as a tumor suppressor.⁠23"
